<title>USA: Gillette sees $80-$120 mln in deal synergies.</title>
<headline>Gillette sees $80-$120 mln in deal synergies.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gillette Co chairman and chief executive Alfred Zeien said the $7 billion planned acquisition of Duracell International Inc is expected to yield $80 to $120 million in savings in two years.</p>
<p>The cost of the merger, the result of talks that began in January, are expected to be $275 million, which is &quot;not a hard number&quot; subject to adjustment, and excludes another $55 million in one-time closing costs.</p>
<p>Zeien also said Warren Buffett, whose Berkshire Hathaway owns 11 percent of Gillette backs the merger, which remains subject to approval by both companies' shareholders.</p>
</text>
